<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <!-- Stone Content Authoring Workbench — xUnit test suite (POC, card t_e2de37e4).
       Strict TDD gate for the Core deep module plus the current-C#↔declarative PARITY proof.

       It references the Core project AND link-compiles the SHIPPED engine-free production
       catalog source (HomesteadProgressionCatalog / FoundationalPieceCatalog / StoneFacets /
       the snapshot codec) exactly as tests/SBPR.Trailborne.Tests.csproj does — so the parity
       adapter reads the REAL current authority through its public interface, with no copied
       second catalog and no source parsing. Every link-compiled file below is free of
       UnityEngine / HarmonyLib / Valheim refs, so it compiles under net8 here.

       The tools/Directory.Build.props shield keeps this subtree out of the repo-root
       Valheim-SDK-path requirement; this suite fetches no Valheim SDK and runs headless. -->

  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFramework>net8.0</TargetFramework>
    <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
    <ImplicitUsings>disable</ImplicitUsings>
    <LangVersion>latest</LangVersion>
    <AssemblyName>StoneContent.Workbench.Tests</AssemblyName>
    <RootNamespace>StoneContent.Workbench.Tests</RootNamespace>
    <IsPackable>false</IsPackable>
    <IsTestProject>true</IsTestProject>
    <TreatWarningsAsErrors>true</TreatWarningsAsErrors>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.NET.Test.Sdk" Version="17.11.1" />
    <PackageReference Include="xunit" Version="2.9.2" />
    <PackageReference Include="xunit.runner.visualstudio" Version="2.8.2">
      <IncludeAssets>runtime; build; native; contentfiles; analyzers; buildtransitive</IncludeAssets>
      <PrivateAssets>all</PrivateAssets>
    </PackageReference>
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="../src/StoneContent.Workbench.Core/StoneContent.Workbench.Core.csproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="../src/StoneContent.Workbench.Web/StoneContent.Workbench.Web.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <!-- SHIPPED, engine-free production catalog source under test (link-compiled, not copied).
       These ARE the current authority; the parity adapter normalizes them into the same
       semantic snapshot as the declarative asset. The repo root sits four levels up. -->
  <ItemGroup>
    <Compile Include="../../../src/SBPR.Niflheim.HomesteadStones/Domain/Snapshots/AggregateSnapshot.cs" />
    <Compile Include="../../../src/SBPR.Niflheim.HomesteadStones/Domain/Content/HomesteadProgressionCatalog.cs" />
    <Compile Include="../../../src/SBPR.Niflheim.HomesteadStones/Domain/Content/FoundationalPieceCatalog.cs" />
    <Compile Include="../../../src/SBPR.Niflheim.HomesteadStones/Domain/StoneProgression/StoneFacets.cs" />
    <!-- StoneFacets.cs pulls in the Stone aggregate + identity types it lives beside. -->
    <Compile Include="../../../src/SBPR.Niflheim.HomesteadStones/Domain/StoneProgression/StoneProgressionAggregate.cs" />
    <Compile Include="../../../src/SBPR.Niflheim.HomesteadStones/Domain/Identity/ProgressionIdentity.cs" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <!-- Canonical asset + schema copied to output so tests read them by relative path. -->
  <ItemGroup>
    <None Include="../assets/homestead-stone.content.json" CopyToOutputDirectory="PreserveNewest" Link="Assets/homestead-stone.content.json" />
    <None Include="../assets/homestead-stone.content.schema.json" CopyToOutputDirectory="PreserveNewest" Link="Assets/homestead-stone.content.schema.json" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <!-- Static frontend copied to output so the tray scroll/resize contract test (t_42b44e70)
       reads the SHIPPED index.html / styles.css / app.js by a stable relative path. -->
  <ItemGroup>
    <None Include="../src/StoneContent.Workbench.Web/wwwroot/index.html" CopyToOutputDirectory="PreserveNewest" Link="Frontend/index.html" />
    <None Include="../src/StoneContent.Workbench.Web/wwwroot/styles.css" CopyToOutputDirectory="PreserveNewest" Link="Frontend/styles.css" />
    <None Include="../src/StoneContent.Workbench.Web/wwwroot/app.js" CopyToOutputDirectory="PreserveNewest" Link="Frontend/app.js" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
